From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:21:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: gpio: apple,smc-gpio: allow the SMC's
 input interrupts

The SMC reports the inputs it watches as events, one line number per
event, and holds the next one for a line until it is acknowledged. Let a
node offer them as interrupts, with two cells (line, type).

The Apple device tree of the MacBook Pro 14-inch (M4, J604) describes the
SD reader's card detect this way: the reader node's interrupt-parent is the
SMC PMU and its interrupt is line 9, so the card can be detected while the
reader's PCIe port is powered down.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml      | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml
index b5159611f7..1748a9e3cc 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/apple,smc-gpio.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,14 @@ properties:
   '#gpio-cells':
     const: 2
 
+  interrupt-controller:
+    description:
+      The SMC reports the inputs it can watch as events; a node with this
+      property offers them as interrupts.
+
+  '#interrupt-cells':
+    const: 2
+
   apple,output-templates:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
     minItems: 2
@@ -40,4 +48,7 @@ required:
   - gpio-controller
   - '#gpio-cells'
 
+dependencies:
+  interrupt-controller: ['#interrupt-cells']
+
 additionalProperties: false
